<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bagendon</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bagendon is a village in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gloucestershire">Gloucestershire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cirencester">Cirencester</a>, beside which lie the earthworks of a large late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> oppidum. Probably a centre of the Dobunni, the site has produced evidence of coin minting and of Roman goods imported in the decades before the Roman conquest of 43 CE. After the conquest the focus of settlement moved to the new Roman town at Cirencester.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bagendon.jpg" alt="Bagendon" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: norman hyett · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bagendon_Church_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1551148.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
